WEBVTT

00:10:28.247 --> 00:10:31.160
one of the challenges
to the success of this movement,

00:10:31.184 --> 00:10:34.424
of getting rid of things like plastic
and helping the economy shift,

00:10:34.448 --> 00:10:37.395
is people look at our movement
with some suspicion.

00:10:37.864 --> 00:10:40.460
And they ask a question,
and the question is:

00:10:40.484 --> 00:10:42.451
How can these people be so passionate?

00:10:43.246 --> 00:10:46.485
A poor person, a low-income person,
somebody in Cancer Alley,

00:10:46.509 --> 00:10:48.943
somebody in Watts,

00:10:48.967 --> 00:10:51.676
somebody in Harlem,
somebody on an Indian reservation,

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:53.918
might say to themselves --
and rightfully so --

00:10:53.942 --> 00:10:55.959
"How can these people be so passionate

00:10:56.848 --> 00:10:58.589
about making sure

00:10:58.613 --> 00:11:02.676
that a plastic bottle
has a second chance in life,